# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUR FAMILY DATA — never commit it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This toolkit is public. Your research is not. Everything below is where
# your own data lands, and all of it is ignored by default.
#
# If you fork this repo to publish your own work, KEEP THESE LINES.
# A GEDCOM from a living family contains birth dates for living people,
# including children. Once pushed to a public remote, it is public forever,
# even if you delete the file in a later commit.

# GEDCOM exports — the raw tree, always contains living people
exports/
*.ged
*.ged.*

# Your scored judgements and research notes
overrides.yaml
overrides.yml

# Archived record images and their manifest
evidence/
!evidence/.gitkeep

# Your research vault (notes, logs, person files)
#
# Anchored to the repo root with a leading slash. Without it, `vault/`
# also matches `templates/vault/` -- which silently excluded the starter
# templates from the published repo and broke setup for every new user.
/vault/
/vault-mirror/
/my-research/

# ...but the starter templates must always ship.
!templates/
!templates/**

# Generated reports — regenerate them, don't commit them
build/
*.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordinary Python / tooling noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
